{"full":"luckyPipewrench/pipelock","name":"pipelock","description":"Open-source AI agent firewall for MCP security and agent egress. Scans mediated HTTP, MCP, A2A, and WebSocket traffic for exfiltration, SSRF, and prompt injection, and emits mediator-signed action receipts: verifiable audit evidence from outside the agent.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":920,"forks":105,"created":"2026-02-08T00:40:18Z","updated":"2026-10-05T16:17:14Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pipelab.org","topics":["agent-security","ai-agent-security","ai-agents","ai-firewall","ai-security","dlp","egress-proxy","github-action","golang","integrity-monitoring","llm-firewall","llm-security","mcp","mcp-security","prompt-injection","security","security-scanning","security-tools","ssrf","ssrf-protection"],"demo":"https://pipelab.org/playground","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:57:09.661Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T16:57:09.661Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T16:57:09.661Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:39:31.421Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:35.848Z","stars":920,"forks":105},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:56.036Z","stars":920,"forks":105},{"at":"2026-10-05T16:57:09.661Z","stars":920,"forks":105}],"technologies":["Go"],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:41.261Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pipelock sits between AI agents and the network. It inspects mediated HTTP, WebSocket, MCP, and A2A traffic, plus CONNECT tunnel contents when TLS interception is enabled, for secret exfiltration, prompt injection, SSRF, tool poisoning, and risky tool-call chains. Plain CONNECT without interception is scanned at the hostname and URL level. Configured MCP upstreams are an exception to private-address SSRF blocking: local/private servers are allowed, but cloud metadata endpoints remain blocked.","Pipelock emits mediator-signed action receipts over content-aware boundary decisions, so a reviewer can verify what Pipelock decided outside the agent runtime. The public agent-egress-bench corpus exercises the detections. The Gauntlet workflow is the product's scheduled candidate exam against a pinned corpus commit; it does not auto-publish a public score. Learn more: Open-source AI firewall.","Works with: Claude Code · OpenAI Codex · Cline · OpenCode · Pi · Zed · Cursor · VS Code · JetBrains · OpenAI Agents SDK · Google ADK · AutoGen · CrewAI · LangGraph"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luckyPipewrench/pipelock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"89aee46fe7507ceefdd90269bb33e3ca8e8a5e3adc8da87fa8828a8992fe4d15","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T05:05:30.403Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:39:31.414Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Pipelock sits between AI agents and the network. It inspects mediated HTTP, WebSocket, MCP, and A2A traffic, plus CONNECT tunnel contents when TLS interception is enabled, for secret exfiltration, prompt injection, SSRF, tool poisoning, and risky tool-call chains. Plain CONNECT without interception is scanned at the hostname and URL level. Configured MCP upstreams are an exception to private-address SSRF blocking: local/private servers are allowed, but cloud metadata endpoints remain blocked.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luckyPipewrench/pipelock/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No account and no server.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luckyPipewrench/pipelock/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"89aee46fe7507ceefdd90269bb33e3ca8e8a5e3adc8da87fa8828a8992fe4d15","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luckyPipewrench/pipelock/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T16:39:31.414Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T16:17:14Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:41:07.036Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v3.6.0","tag":"v3.6.0","publishedAt":"2026-10-03T00:41:55Z","url":"https://github.com/luckyPipewrench/pipelock/releas